<article class="env-remark" id="03P0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03P0">Remark <span data-tag="03P0">59.22.2</span>.</a> In the statement of Lemma <a href="/tag/03OZ" data-tag="03OZ">59.22.1</a> the covering $\mathcal{U}$ is a refinement of $\mathcal{V}$ but not the other way around. Coverings of the form $\{ V \to U\} $ do not form an initial subcategory of the category of all coverings of $U$. Yet it is still true that we can compute Čech cohomology $\check H^ n(U, \mathcal{F})$ (which is defined as the colimit over the opposite of the category of coverings $\mathcal{U}$ of $U$ of the Čech cohomology groups of $\mathcal{F}$ with respect to $\mathcal{U}$) in terms of the coverings $\{ V \to U\} $. We will formulate a precise lemma (it only works for sheaves) and add it here if we ever need it. </p>
